flowchart TB
    accTitle: Query agent safeguards — enforced checks and remaining limits
    accDescr: Four panels distinguish code-enforced request and SQL checks, bounded execution and failure behavior, prompt-guided behavior, and data/privacy limitations. Inputs and history are validated, MCP is isolated by per-turn IDs, generated SQL is rechecked and executed unchanged in read-only transactions, and duplicate work is memoized. Six loop model calls exclude generation and summary. WebSocket turns and MCP calls have separate 180-second limits, while database statement and lock timeouts are 10 and 3 seconds. History and results are bounded, cancellation is cooperative, and model providers receive unredacted loaded rows. Read-only checks do not provide authentication, per-user authorization, or a general function sandbox.
    %% Four independent panels; arrows order the cards within each panel.
    %% Source references and reading guide: mermaid/README.md

    subgraph INPUT["1. Request and MCP checks — enforced in code"]
        direction LR
        I1["WebSocket question: 1–10,000 characters. History: alternating user/assistant pairs; at most 40 messages and 120,000 characters"]:::work
        I2["MCP schemas validate inputs and outputs. Application adds a UUID; each call resolves only its active turn context"]:::work
        I3["Credentials and callbacks stay on the server. Shared MCP connection uses in-memory transport; context deleted in finally"]:::work
        I1 --> I2 --> I3
    end

    subgraph SQL["2. SQL and database checks — enforced in code"]
        direction LR
        S1["Accept one SELECT-based query with recognized table references. Allow SELECT CTEs; check connected-schema table allow-list"]:::data
        S2["Reject writes, DDL, write CTEs, SELECT INTO, row locks, and multiple statements. Execution must match saved validated SQL"]:::data
        S3["Database rechecks policy; READ ONLY transaction; fixed search path. Statement timeout: 10 seconds; lock timeout: 3 seconds"]:::data
        S1 --> S2 --> S3
    end

    subgraph WORK["3. Work and failure limits — enforced in code"]
        direction LR
        W1["At most 6 agent-loop model calls; generation and summary calls are extra. Stop after execution or a tool failure"]:::work
        W2["Reuse per-turn operation promises, including failures; no automatic provider retry. Query failure ends turn; summary-only failure keeps table + warning"]:::work
        W3["WebSocket turn: 180 seconds; each MCP call: 180 seconds. Cancel signals propagate; active SQL may run until completion or DB timeout"]:::note
        W1 --> W2 --> W3
    end

    subgraph LIMITS["4. Answer and data boundaries — limits remain"]
        direction LR
        L1["Prompt guidance: clarify ambiguity; treat history and rows as data; answer only from available facts. Model compliance and correctness are not guaranteed"]:::note
        L2["At most 1,000 loaded rows per query; count is not total matches. Retained history keeps all rows, dropping whole turns to fit; older facts may be missing"]:::note
        L3["Real AI receives questions, schema, and loaded rows without redaction. Public demo has no login or per-user policy; DB role controls table/function access"]:::note
        L1 --> L2 --> L3
    end

    INPUT ~~~ SQL
    SQL ~~~ WORK
    WORK ~~~ LIMITS

